      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T19:06:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest saving weak_ptr\u003c\u003e instead. This has something to do with \"ownership\" of an object. Only owner needs strong reference/pointer to the object.\n\nPointerControllerContext should be owned by PointerController only so we should only save weak pointer to it here.\n\nIn Chrome sometimes we don\u0027t even use pointers. We just use the value type in the owner and let other classes hold reference types. However since Handler and Callback use weak_ptr, I\u0027ll defer to the original design and use weak_ptr here instead.",
      "range": {
